# Test Integrity (Mandatory)

Full rationale: `doc/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN_REGRESSION_RESILIENCE.md` §3–§4.

## When a test fails, classify it first

| Class | Meaning | Allowed action |
| ----- | ------- | -------------- |
| `stale_test` | Test no longer compiles / matches a renamed type or field; product semantics unchanged | Fix the test without changing what it asserts |
| `flake` / `non_hermetic` | Env race, network, local `data/`, wall clock | Isolate (`test_env::EnvGuard`, tempdir, injected clock, localhost mock). **No** retries, **no** wider time windows |
| `economic_regression` | Golden / invariant diff on PnL, IL, fees, balances, sizing, lineage | **Stop and ask the user.** It is either a bug or a deliberate change explained in a "Golden delta" section |
| `assertion_weakened` | Deleting a test/snapshot, number → `is_ok()`, loosening tolerance, adding `#[ignore]` to get green | **Forbidden** |
| `infra` | Missing script, wrong workflow ref, CI tooling | Fix the infra |

State the class in your message when you touch a failing test.

## Rules

1. **Hermetic:** active tests use no network (except localhost mocks), no repo `data/`, no `set_current_dir`; env mutation only through the crate's `test_env::EnvGuard`. `RpcConfig { .. Default::default() }` in tests needs `fallback_urls: Vec::new()`. Repair jobs on real data = `#[ignore = "manual: ..."]`.
2. **No vacuous pass:** a test must not `return` early without asserting; required resources (DB) fail instead of skip when `CLMM_REQUIRE_DB_TESTS=1`.
3. **Goldens / snapshots / expected numbers are not edited to make CI green.** Update only via local `cargo insta review` in the same PR, with a **"Golden delta: what changed and why"** section in the PR description.
4. **New feature = tests in the same PR**, per the wave map in §7 of the resilience plan. Changing a critical file (list in `scripts/ci/critical-area-test-gate.sh`) without test changes fails CI; label `no-tests-needed` is only for pure refactors/comments, with the reason in the PR body.
5. **New numeric logic in web** goes to `web/src/lib/*.ts` with a test, not into a page component.
6. **New plan document** (`IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN_*`, `ROADMAP_*`, `*_PLAN.md`) must contain a "Testy i kryteria regresji" section (template: `doc/templates/TEST_SECTION.md`). A plan without it is incomplete.
7. Before pushing: `cargo fmt --all`; full check = `make verify` / `tools/verify.ps1` (the pre-push hook runs it).
